From: Rob Lymm <rob@mediaeden.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: do not report submission statistics the GPU never wrote

retire_submit() reads a per-submission statistics slot out of the ring's
memptrs and reports the elapsed time and CP clock from it. Those fields are
written by the GPU as it runs the submission, but only a6xx emits the
packets that write them: a3xx and a4xx have no always-on counter and write
nothing there.

Nothing clears the slot either, and it is reused every
MSM_GPU_SUBMIT_STATS_COUNT submissions, so on those generations it holds
whatever was last in that memory. Without an IOMMU the ring comes out of
the VRAM carveout, which is not zeroed, and the values are wild. On an
Adreno 330:

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -654,6 +654,25 @@
  * Cmdstream submission/retirement:
  */
 
+/*
+ * The submission statistics are memory the GPU writes as it runs the
+ * submission. Not every generation writes them: A3XX and A4XX have no
+ * always-on counter and emit nothing here. The slot is reused every
+ * MSM_GPU_SUBMIT_STATS_COUNT submissions, so left alone it holds whatever
+ * the previous owner of that memory left behind, and retire reports it as
+ * an elapsed time. Clear it before the GPU runs the submission.
+ */
+static void clear_submit_stats(struct msm_ringbuffer *ring, uint32_t seqno)
+{
+	volatile struct msm_gpu_submit_stats *stats =
+		&ring->memptrs->stats[seqno % MSM_GPU_SUBMIT_STATS_COUNT];
+
+	stats->cpcycles_start = 0;
+	stats->cpcycles_end   = 0;
+	stats->alwayson_start = 0;
+	stats->alwayson_end   = 0;
+}
+
 static void retire_submit(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct msm_ringbuffer *ring,
 		struct msm_gem_submit *submit)
 {
@@ -769,6 +788,8 @@
 
 	submit->seqno = submit->hw_fence->seqno;
 
+	clear_submit_stats(ring, submit->seqno);
+
 	update_sw_cntrs(gpu);
 
 	/*
